    {:category :function,
     :zig-version "0.16.0",
     :symbol aguafria.std.fs.path/relativePosix,
     :name "relativePosix",
     :signature
     "pub fn relativePosix(allocator: Allocator, cwd: []const u8, from: []const u8, to: []const u8) Allocator.Error![]u8",
     :param-count 4,
     :source "std/fs/path.zig",
     :zig-name "@import(\"std\").fs.path.relativePosix",
     :documentation
     "Returns the non-absolute path from from to to according to Windows rules.\n\nOther than memory allocation, this is a pure function; the result solely\ndepends on the input parameters.\n\nIf from and to each resolve to the same path (after calling resolve\non each), a zero-length string is returned.",
     :clojure-name "relativePosix",
     :container false,
     :alias-depth 0}
    {:category :function,
     :zig-version "0.16.0",
     :symbol aguafria.std.fs.path/relativeWindows,
     :name "relativeWindows",
     :signature
     "pub fn relativeWindows( gpa: Allocator, cwd: []const u8, environ_map: ?*const std.process.Environ.Map, from: []const u8, to: []const u8, ) Allocator.Error![]u8",
     :param-count 5,
     :source "std/fs/path.zig",
     :zig-name "@import(\"std\").fs.path.relativeWindows",
     :documentation
     "Returns the non-absolute path from from to to according to Windows rules.\n\nOther than memory allocation, this is a pure function; the result solely\ndepends on the input parameters.\n\nIf from and to each resolve to the same path (after calling resolve\non each), a zero-length string is returned.\n\nThe result is not guaranteed to be relative, as the paths may be on\ndifferent volumes. In that case, the result will be the canonicalized\nabsolute path of to.\n\nPer-drive CWDs are stored in special semi-hidden environment variables of\nthe format =<drive-letter>:, e.g. =C:. This type of CWD is purely a\nshell concept, so there's no guarantee that it'll be set or that it'll even\nbe accurate. This is the only reason for the environ_map parameter. null is\ntreated equivalent to the environment variable missing.",
     :clojure-name "relativeWindows",
     :container false,
     :alias-depth 0}
    {:category :function,
     :zig-version "0.16.0",
     :symbol aguafria.std.fs.path/resolve,
     :name "resolve",
     :signature
     "pub fn resolve(allocator: Allocator, paths: []const []const u8) Allocator.Error![]u8",
     :param-count 2,
     :source "std/fs/path.zig",
     :zig-name "@import(\"std\").fs.path.resolve",
     :documentation
     "On Windows, this calls resolveWindows and on POSIX it calls resolvePosix.",
     :clojure-name "resolve",
     :container false,
     :alias-depth 0}
    {:category :function,
     :zig-version "0.16.0",
     :symbol aguafria.std.fs.path/resolvePosix,
     :name "resolvePosix",
     :signature
     "pub fn resolvePosix(allocator: Allocator, paths: []const []const u8) Allocator.Error![]u8",
     :param-count 2,
     :source "std/fs/path.zig",
     :zig-name "@import(\"std\").fs.path.resolvePosix",
     :documentation
     "This function is like a series of cd statements executed one after another.\n\nIt resolves \".\" and \"..\" to the best of its ability, but will not convert relative paths to\nan absolute path, use Io.Dir.realpath instead.\n\n\"..\" components may persist in the resolved path if the resolved path is relative.\n\nThe result does not have a trailing path separator.\n\nThis function does not perform any syscalls. Executing this series of path\nlookups on the actual filesystem may produce different results due to\nsymlinks.",
     :clojure-name "resolvePosix",
     :container false,
     :alias-depth 0}
    {:category :function,
     :zig-version "0.16.0",
     :symbol aguafria.std.fs.path/resolveWindows,
     :name "resolveWindows",
     :signature
     "pub fn resolveWindows(allocator: Allocator, paths: []const []const u8) Allocator.Error![]u8",
     :param-count 2,
     :source "std/fs/path.zig",
     :zig-name "@import(\"std\").fs.path.resolveWindows",
     :documentation
     "This function is like a series of cd statements executed one after another.\nIt resolves \".\" and \"..\" to the best of its ability, but will not convert relative paths to\nan absolute path, use Io.Dir.realpath instead.\n\"..\" components may persist in the resolved path if the resolved path is relative or drive-relative.\nPath separators are canonicalized to '\\' and drives are canonicalized to capital letters.\n\nThe result will not have a trailing path separator, except for the following scenarios:\n\nThe resolved path is drive-absolute with no components (e.g. C:\\).\n\nThe resolved path is a UNC path with only a server name, and the input path contained a trailing separator\n(e.g. \\\\server\\).\n\nThe resolved path is a UNC path with no components after the share name, and the input path contained a\ntrailing separator (e.g. \\\\server\\share\\).\n\nEach drive has its own current working directory, which is only resolved via the paths provided.\nIn the scenario that the resolved path contains a drive-relative path that can't be resolved using the paths alone,\nthe result will be a drive-relative path.\nSimilarly, in the scenario that the resolved path contains a rooted path that can't be resolved using the paths alone,\nthe result will be a rooted path.\n\nNote: all usage of this function should be audited due to the existence of symlinks.\nWithout performing actual syscalls, resolving .. could be incorrect.\nThis API may break in the future: https://github.com/ziglang/zig/issues/13613",
     :clojure-name "resolveWindows",
     :container false,
     :alias-depth 0}
