     :symbol aguafria.std.http.Server.Request/readerExpectContinue,
     :name "readerExpectContinue",
     :signature
     "pub fn readerExpectContinue(request: *Request, buffer: []u8) ExpectContinueError!*Reader",
     :param-count 2,
     :source "std/http/Server.zig",
     :zig-name
     "@import(\"std\").http.Server.Request.readerExpectContinue",
     :documentation
     "In the case that the request contains \"expect: 100-continue\", this\nfunction writes the continuation header, which means it can fail with a\nwrite error. After sending the continuation header, it sets the\nrequest's expect field to null.\n\nAsserts that this function is only called once.\n\nSee readerExpectNone for an infallible alternative that cannot write\nto the server output stream.",
