     :param-count 2,
     :source "std/http/Server.zig",
     :zig-name "@import(\"std\").http.Server.Request.readerExpectNone",
     :documentation
     "Asserts the expect header is null. The caller must handle the\nexpectation manually and then set the value to null prior to calling\nthis function.\n\nAsserts that this function is only called once.\n\nInvalidates the string memory inside Head.",
     :clojure-name "readerExpectNone",
     :container false,
     :alias-depth 0}
    {:category :function,
     :zig-version "0.16.0",
     :symbol aguafria.std.http.Server.Request/respond,
     :name "respond",
     :signature
     "pub fn respond( request: *Request, content: []const u8, options: RespondOptions, ) ExpectContinueError!void",
     :param-count 3,
     :source "std/http/Server.zig",
     :zig-name "@import(\"std\").http.Server.Request.respond",
     :documentation
     "Send an entire HTTP response to the client, including headers and body.\n\nAutomatically handles HEAD requests by omitting the body.\n\nUnless transfer_encoding is specified, uses the \"content-length\"\nheader.\n\nIf the request contains a body and the connection is to be reused,\ndiscards the request body, leaving the Server in the ready state. If\nthis discarding fails, the connection is marked as not to be reused and\nno error is surfaced.\n\nAsserts status is not continue.\nAsserts that \"\\r\\n\" does not occur in any header name or value.",
     :clojure-name "respond",
     :container false,
     :alias-depth 0}
    {:category :function,
     :zig-version "0.16.0",
     :symbol aguafria.std.http.Server.Request/respondStreaming,
     :name "respondStreaming",
     :signature
     "pub fn respondStreaming( request: *Request, buffer: []u8, options: RespondStreamingOptions, ) ExpectContinueError!http.BodyWriter",
     :param-count 3,
     :source "std/http/Server.zig",
     :zig-name "@import(\"std\").http.Server.Request.respondStreaming",
     :documentation
     "The header is not guaranteed to be sent until BodyWriter.flush or\nBodyWriter.end is called.\n\nIf the request contains a body and the connection is to be reused,\ndiscards the request body, leaving the Server in the ready state. If\nthis discarding fails, the connection is marked as not to be reused and\nno error is surfaced.\n\nHEAD requests are handled transparently by setting the\nBodyWriter.elide flag on the returned BodyWriter, causing\nthe response stream to omit the body. However, it may be worth noticing\nthat flag and skipping any expensive work that would otherwise need to\nbe done to satisfy the request.\n\nAsserts status is not continue.",
     :clojure-name "respondStreaming",
     :container false,
     :alias-depth 0}
    {:category :function,
     :zig-version "0.16.0",
     :symbol aguafria.std.http.Server.Request/respondUnflushed,
