    {:category :function,
     :zig-version "0.16.0",
     :symbol aguafria.std.Io.Future/cancel,
     :name "cancel",
     :signature "pub fn cancel(f: *@This(), io: Io) Result",
     :param-count 2,
     :source "std/Io.zig",
     :zig-name "@import(\"std\").Io.Future.cancel",
     :documentation
     "Equivalent to await but places a cancelation request. This causes the task to receive\nerror.Canceled from its next \"cancelation point\" (if any). A cancelation point is a\ncall to a function in Io which can return error.Canceled.\n\nAfter cancelation of a task is requested, only the next cancelation point in that task\nwill return error.Canceled: future points will not re-signal the cancelation. As such,\nit is usually a bug to ignore error.Canceled. However, to defer handling cancelation\nrequests, see also recancel and CancelProtection.\n\nIdempotent. Not threadsafe.",
     :clojure-name "cancel",
     :container false,
     :alias-depth 0}],
   :name aguafria.std.Io.Future,
   :zig-path ["Io" "Future"]}
  {:zig-name "@import(\"std\").Io.Group",
   :documentation
   "An unordered set of tasks which can only be awaited or canceled as a whole.\nTasks are spawned in the group with Group.async and Group.concurrent.\n\nThe resources associated with each task are guaranteed to be released when\nthe individual task returns, as opposed to when the whole group completes or\nis awaited. For this reason, it is not a resource leak to have a long-lived\ngroup which concurrent tasks are repeatedly added to. However, asynchronous\ntasks are not guaranteed to run until Group.await or Group.cancel is\ncalled, so adding async tasks to a group without ever awaiting it may leak\nresources.",
   :source "std/Io.zig",
   :members
   [{:category :function,
     :zig-version "0.16.0",
     :symbol aguafria.std.Io.Group/async,
     :name "async",
     :signature
     "pub fn async(g: *Group, io: Io, function: anytype, args: std.meta.ArgsTuple(@TypeOf(function))) void",
     :param-count 3,
     :source "std/Io.zig",
     :zig-name "@import(\"std\").Io.Group.async",
     :documentation
     "Equivalent to Io.async, except the task is spawned in this Group\ninstead of becoming associated with a Future.\n\nThe return type of function must be coercible to Cancelable!void.\nfunction returning error.Canceled does nothing because it is an\ncancelation propagation boundary.\n\nOnce this function is called, there are resources associated with the\ngroup. To release those resources, Group.await or Group.cancel must\neventually be called.",
     :clojure-name "async",
     :container false,
     :alias-depth 0}
    {:category :function,
     :zig-version "0.16.0",
     :symbol aguafria.std.Io.Group/await,
     :name "await",
     :signature "pub fn await(g: *Group, io: Io) Cancelable!void",
     :param-count 2,
     :source "std/Io.zig",
     :zig-name "@import(\"std\").Io.Group.await",
     :documentation
     "Blocks until all tasks of the group finish. During this time,\ncancelation requests propagate to all members of the group, and\nwill also cause error.Canceled to be returned when the group\ndoes ultimately finish.\n\nIdempotent. Not threadsafe.\n\nIt is safe to call this function concurrently with Group.async or\nGroup.concurrent, provided that the group does not complete until\nthe call to Group.async or Group.concurrent returns.",
     :clojure-name "await",
     :container false,
     :alias-depth 0}
    {:category :function,
     :zig-version "0.16.0",
     :symbol aguafria.std.Io.Group/cancel,
     :name "cancel",
     :signature "pub fn cancel(g: *Group, io: Io) void",
     :param-count 2,
     :source "std/Io.zig",
     :zig-name "@import(\"std\").Io.Group.cancel",
     :documentation
     "Equivalent to await but immediately requests cancelation on all\nmembers of the group.\n\nFor a description of cancelation and cancelation points, see Future.cancel.\n\nIdempotent. Not threadsafe.\n\nIt is safe to call this function concurrently with Group.async or\nGroup.concurrent, provided that the group does not complete until\nthe call to Group.async or Group.concurrent returns.",
     :clojure-name "cancel",
     :container false,
     :alias-depth 0}
    {:category :function,
