    {:category :function,
     :zig-version "0.16.0",
     :symbol aguafria.std.Io.Queue/close,
     :name "close",
     :signature "pub fn close(q: *@This(), io: Io) void",
     :param-count 2,
     :source "std/Io.zig",
     :zig-name "@import(\"std\").Io.Queue.close",
     :documentation
     "After this is called, the queue enters a \"closed\" state. A closed\nqueue always returns error.Closed for put attempts even when\nthere is space in the buffer. However, existing elements of the\nqueue are retrieved before error.Closed is returned.\n\nThreadsafe.",
     :clojure-name "close",
     :container false,
     :alias-depth 0}
    {:category :function,
     :zig-version "0.16.0",
     :symbol aguafria.std.Io.Queue/get,
     :name "get",
     :signature
     "pub fn get(q: *@This(), io: Io, buffer: []Elem, min: usize) (QueueClosedError || Cancelable)!usize",
     :param-count 4,
     :source "std/Io.zig",
     :zig-name "@import(\"std\").Io.Queue.get",
     :documentation
     "Receives elements from the beginning of the queue, potentially blocking\nif there are insufficient elements currently in the queue. Returns when\nany one of the following conditions is satisfied:\n\nAt least min elements have been received from the queue\n\nThe queue is closed and contains no buffered elements\n\nThe current task is canceled\n\nReturns how many elements of buffer have been populated, if any.\nIf an error is returned, no elements have been populated.\n\nIf the queue is closed or the task is canceled, but some items were\nalready received before the closure or cancelation, then get may\nreturn a number lower than min, in which case future calls are\nguaranteed to return error.Canceled or error.Closed.\n\nA return value of 0 is only possible if min is 0, in which case\nthe call is guaranteed to fill as much of buffer as is possible\nwithout blocking.\n\nAsserts that buffer.len >= min.",
     :clojure-name "get",
     :container false,
     :alias-depth 0}
    {:category :function,
     :zig-version "0.16.0",
     :symbol aguafria.std.Io.Queue/getOne,
