    {:category :function,
     :zig-version "0.16.0",
     :symbol aguafria.std.mem.Allocator/remap,
     :name "remap",
     :signature
     "pub fn remap(self: Allocator, allocation: anytype, new_len: usize) ?@TypeOf(allocation)",
     :param-count 2,
     :source "std/mem/Allocator.zig",
     :zig-name "@import(\"std\").mem.Allocator.remap",
     :documentation
     "Request to modify the size of an allocation, allowing relocation.\n\nA non-null return value indicates the resize was successful. The\nallocation may have same address, or may have been relocated. In either\ncase, the allocation now has size of new_len. A null return value\nindicates that the resize would be equivalent to allocating new memory,\ncopying the bytes from the old memory, and then freeing the old memory.\nIn such case, it is more efficient for the caller to perform those\noperations.\n\nallocation may be an empty slice, in which case null is returned,\nunless new_len is also 0, in which case allocation is returned.\n\nnew_len may be zero, in which case the allocation is freed.\n\nIf the allocation's elements' type is zero bytes sized, allocation.len is set to new_len.",
     :clojure-name "remap",
     :container false,
     :alias-depth 0}
    {:category :function,
     :zig-version "0.16.0",
     :symbol aguafria.std.mem.Allocator/resize,
     :name "resize",
     :signature
     "pub fn resize(self: Allocator, allocation: anytype, new_len: usize) bool",
     :param-count 2,
     :source "std/mem/Allocator.zig",
     :zig-name "@import(\"std\").mem.Allocator.resize",
     :documentation
     "Request to modify the size of an allocation.\n\nIt is guaranteed to not move the pointer, however the allocator\nimplementation may refuse the resize request by returning false.\n\nallocation may be an empty slice, in which case false is returned,\nunless new_len is also 0, in which case true is returned.\n\nnew_len may be zero, in which case the allocation is freed.",
